  "_comment": "German-pivot repair for the risk-register glossary. These are AGENT DRAFTS, not reviewed translations: they do not close a localization-work item and each pack needs a native pass before the pack is called Tier-1 complete. They are landed anyway because the alternative is shipping raw German -- Wahrscheinlichkeit, Auswirkung, Akzeptanz, Risikoregister -- to operators who do not read German, which is the worse of the two states. Terminology decisions: 'Record' is the submit verb (German 'Erfassen' confirms the verb reading, not the noun), 'Likelihood' uses each language's risk-assessment term rather than a general 'possibility', and 'Risk Register' reuses each pack's own existing risks:title wording where that key is itself clean. nl/sv treatment of 'Titel' is excluded as a genuine shared cognate rather than a leak.",
